 \subsection{Deviations}
 \label{sec:exp003-deviations}
 
-(1) An encoding error in the analysis and scoring code mis-keyed non-ASCII nouns; it was fixed before the controls were evaluated and before any main-stage sample existed, and the pilot analysis, which served for sizing only, may carry it. PC-1 then failed and the main stage continued as the card allows, under W2. (2) Eleven interpretive readings of the card and one erratum were accepted before scoring; the erratum corrects the mechanism paragraph, since the unconditional guidance branch masks every observed position and not only the prefix. (3) The hard stop on GPU time was raised from 7.0 to 8.5 hours, with the user's approval, during generation and before any main-stage sample was scored; the run used 8.02 hours against a plan of 6. (4) The pilot freeze was re-recorded for one analysis file, after generation and before scoring, for the encoding fix and a change of line endings. (5) A scoring-driver progress check that looked in the wrong directory stopped scoring falsely; it was fixed and scoring resumed. (6) The frozen analysis omitted five items, computed afterwards and labelled post-freeze: guardrail (iv), the composition contrast, the diversity intervals, the achieved detectable effect, and the counts of undersized placebo pools; three secondary contrasts used 5,000 bootstrap replicates, not 10,000. The gate audit verified the freeze hashes and the order of events, reproduced the confirmatory file byte for byte, and found no deviation that a main-stage outcome could have influenced. The evidence is a single preregistered run, and its outputs are not yet archived.\todo{archive runs/EXP-003 (untracked in the worktree that ran it) with the code and give the DOI; generated images are withheld because UniDisc states no licence} % src: decisions D0017, D0018, D0022, D0023, D0024, D0025; A sections 1.2 to 1.4 and 3; runs/EXP-003/clock.json
